{"name":"Cobblestone Street","hex":"#cfc7b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cobblestone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rounded stone from a river bed, fit for use as ballast in ships and for paving roads.","Cobblestones viewed as a building or paving material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cobblestone"},{"term":"street","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paved part of road, usually in a village or a town.","A road as above, but including the sidewalks (pavements) and buildings."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build or equip with streets.","To eject; to throw onto the streets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/street"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cobblestone Street","blocks":[{"text":"Cobblestone Street is the seventh solo album by former White Lion and Freak of Nature lead singer, Mike Tramp, released April 8, 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0a/MTramp_Cobblestone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobblestone_Street"},{"title":"Cobblestone Street (Boonville, Missouri)","blocks":[{"text":"Cobblestone Street, also known as Fifth Street and Main Street, is a historic cobblestone street located at Boonville, Cooper County, Missouri. It was built about 1832, and was part of the original Fifth or Main Street. It is located beneath the Boonville Road Bridge and is constructed of cobblestones of varying sizes. The street remnant is approximately 20 feet wide and approximately 200 feet long. The street connected the main commercial district of Boonville with the wharves along the Missouri River."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/COBBLESTONE_STREET%2C_BOONVILLE%2C_COOPER_COUNTY%2C_MO.JPG/330px-COBBLESTONE_STREET%2C_BOONVILLE%2C_COOPER_COUNTY%2C_MO.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobblestone_Street_(Boonville%2C_Missouri)"},{"title":"List of cobblestone streets","blocks":[{"text":"A cobbled street or cobblestone road, is a street or road paved with cobblestones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Cleaning_the_cobbles_at_Church_of_Santo_Domingo_de_Guzm%C3%A1n_%288263583297%29.jpg/330px-Cleaning_the_cobbles_at_Church_of_Santo_Domingo_de_Guzm%C3%A1n_%288263583297%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_cobblestone_streets"},{"title":"Cobblestone","blocks":[{"text":"Cobblestone is a natural building material based on cobble-sized stones, and is used for pavement roads, streets, and buildings. Setts, also called Belgian blocks, are often referred to as \"cobbles\", although a sett is distinct from a cobblestone by being quarried and shaped into a regular form, while cobblestones are naturally occurring rounded forms less uniform in size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ancient_road_surface.jpg/330px-Ancient_road_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobblestone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Cobblestone_J1.JPG/500px-Cobblestone_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Cobblestone_J1.JPG/1280px-Cobblestone_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Cobblestone_J1.JPG/500px-Cobblestone_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sett block, sometimes mistakenly referred to as a cobble, but distinguished by being quarried & carved rather than naturally occurring, and being of regular size and rectangular shape.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACobblestone_J1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Guzow-oryszew_road_cm04.jpg/500px-Guzow-oryszew_road_cm04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Guzow-oryszew_road_cm04.jpg/500px-Guzow-oryszew_road_cm04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuzow-oryszew_road_cm04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg/120px-ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg/250px-ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg/120px-ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalianStones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg/500px-Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg/1280px-Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg/500px-Sint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASint-Kornelis-Horebeke_-_Haaghoek_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Carrefour_de_l